  "label": "User projected onto the prisoners as an example of happiness",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the prisoners in the image, who are depicted smiling and raising their hands. The text 'you can be happy and' directly addresses the user ('you'), implying that the viewer should emulate the prisoners' happiness, despite the horrific context of their imprisonment. This projection equates the viewer with the prisoners, suggesting the viewer can adopt their demeanor as a model for happiness in any situation, which is a harmful and misleading interpretation.",
